# Log files: never block a merge/rebase/stash-pop on a conflict.
# `union` is a built-in git merge driver (no per-machine config needed, so it
# works on every clone and in CI) — it takes the lines from BOTH sides instead
# of raising a conflict. Build logs are regenerated on the next run anyway, so
# the only cost is a briefly duplicated log body; the win is the pre-push hook's
# `pull --rebase --autostash` never gets stuck half-way (see the stuck
# .git/rebase-merge incident).
*.log merge=union
